             ***The Shadow's EdGe Chat Line Editor V1.0***
          For CNet3.0/3.05 (Not yet tested with other Versions)
                               By FishBone



                            ***What Is It?***

	This is a little program I wrote on a request from a friend.  It allows
the SysOp to change the line that appears when a user enters a chat request &
the SysOp is unavailable.  It will save multiple lines to use, allowing you to 
select any line at any time, or you can choose to have them all randomly 
displayed.


                          ***Files Included***

	Files That should be in this archive:

	   Chat/Chat
		The Main program

	   Chat/Chat.Ran
		The program Used if Random Mode is selected

	   Chat/Not
		This is the file that is read when a user requests chat with 
		the SysOp and he is unavailable.  When you select a new line to
                use, it is copied here.

	   Chat/1
		A starter line so the program will work right off the bat, if
		you don't want to edit/add new lines right away.  Every line
		you save will be saved as a Number. (i.e. 1,2,3,etc...)

	   Chat/List
		This is an important file!  DO NOT REMOVE!!!  It contains the
		total Number of lines you have saved.  the program will update
		it everytime you add or Delete a line.  If this file becomes 
		Corrupt then the program will start doing strange things!

	   ShadEdGe.Gif
		A blatant (not to mention Shameless) ad for My BBs!


                           ***Installation***

	O.K., this is fairly painless.  First, copy the entire Chat directory
to the SysText: Directory, (the chat directory MUST reside in SysText: for the 
program to work !!!)  Then load your BBsText file into a text editor and
change go to 161 (At least that is the line in my CNet 3.05, yours may vary.)
The stock CNet version should Read:
               
                 \n1Sorry, the Sysop is not available.\n1

                    NOTE: all "\" above are CONTROL-Y

	You may have changed it, But it probably still has the same jist.
Now change Line 161 so it now reads

                     \n1{*0systext:chat/not}\n1
                    
        NOTE: all "\" above are CONTROL-Y and all "{" are CONTROL-Q


	Then Load your BBsMenu into a text editor.  At the end of:

            1; Maintenance Menu

	Add the Line:

            CHATED   `31   |{#0systext:chat/chat}

                  NOTE:  The above "{" is a CONTROL-Q 
        NOTE:  The `31 above is the access groups allowed to use the
	     Program.  Change to suit your BBs!  (i.e. `25-31, etc...)
	
	That's it!!  The program is now ready to Run!!


                              ***Usage***

	The program itself is fairly straight-forward.  If you Installed it
as explained above, then type "chated" from anywhere to start the program.
      **NOTE**  This can also be adopted to your SysOp only PFiles/GFiles
	               as an arexx program.
	Select a Line to use a line you already have saved, Create to create a
new line, Edit to change a line you alredy have saved, Kill to delete a saved
line, View to see 1 or all of the lines you have saved, & Random to enable
Random Mode which will randomly Display all of your saved lines.
	When you choose "Create" or "Edit" you will be directed to your default
editor. 

                               ***NOTE!***
	You can use all available Mci Commands inside a line, I have tested it
With them all (Including the % command, just to see if it would work!) and
there is no limit as to how Many lines each entry can contain!  The program
does limit you to 20 separate entries, as this is the maximum # of lines I have
tested it with.
 


